    "PROJECT_NAME": "Panelarr",
    "PROJECT_SLUG": "panelarr",
    "PROJECT_PITCH": "A self-hosted, arr-style app for curating, downloading, managing and reading manga, manhwa, manhua and comics, with real multi-user support and opt-in plugins for sources and metadata.",
    "OWNER": "@aurimasniekis",
    "KEEPER_SESSION": "panelarr-knowledge",
    "TODAY": "2026-10-11",
    "KB_COMMIT_POLICY": "the keeper commits on its own after each discussion",
    "KB_PUSH_POLICY": "never by the agent",
    "AREAS_TABLE": "| Folder | Holds | Question it answers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `product/` | Vision, principles, scope, personas | Why and what are we building, for whom? |\n| `architecture/` | Cross-repo design: overview, domain model, deployment, security, repo standard | How do the pieces fit together? |\n| `modules/` | One sub-folder per repo: role, boundaries, internals, implementation status | How is each repo built and what does it own? |\n| `contracts/` | The reasoning behind APIs, protocols and file formats between repos | Why does each interface look the way it does? |\n| `research/` | Facts about external projects, libraries, standards | What exists out there, and what did we learn? |\n| `planning/` | Roadmap, milestones, features with acceptance criteria, releases, status reports | What gets delivered, and when? |\n| `agents/` | Coding-session board, goal briefs, inbox for session messages | Who is working on what? |\n| `qa/` | Test plans, test reports, regression list | Does it work, and how do we know? |\n| `support/` | FAQ, known issues, reusable replies | What do users ask, and what do we answer? |\n| `ops/` | Forge digests and the outbox of drafted comments and reviews | What's happening on the forges? |\n| `playbooks/` | How the agent performs each role | How does the agent do its job? |\n| `decisions/` | Decision records (ADRs) | What did we decide, and what did we reject? |\n| `questions/` | Open-question register | What don't we know yet? |\n| `inputs/` | The owner's words, verbatim and immutable | Where did an idea come from? |\n| `journal/` | One entry per working session | What happened in each session? |\n| `meta/` | Conventions, commit convention, protocols, authority, glossary, templates | How does this KB work? |",
    "DOMAIN_COMMIT_TYPES": "Domain types for this KB:\n\n| Type | Use when… |\n|---|---|\n| `product` | Vision, principles, scope, personas |\n| `arch` | Cross-repo architecture |\n| `module` | One repo's design or status |\n| `contract` | Reasoning behind an API, protocol or format |\n| `research` | Facts about external projects or data |",
    "SETUP_ANSWERS": "```json\n{\n  \"project\": {\n    \"name\": \"Panelarr\",\n    \"pitch\": \"A self-hosted, arr-style app for curating, downloading, managing and reading manga, manhwa, manhua and comics, with real multi-user support and opt-in plugins for sources and metadata.\",\n    \"owner\": \"@aurimasniekis\",\n    \"keeper_session\": \"panelarr-knowledge\",\n    \"slug\": \"panelarr\",\n    \"language\": \"en\"\n  },\n  \"preset\": \"platform\",\n  \"mode\": \"agents\",\n  \"roles\": {\n    \"product_owner\": true,\n    \"project_manager\": true,\n    \"agent_manager\": true,\n    \"qa\": true,\n    \"docs_writer\": true,\n    \"support\": true\n  },\n  \"agents\": [\n    \"claude\"\n  ],\n  \"repos\": [],\n  \"authority\": {\n    \"kb_commit\": \"auto\",\n    \"kb_push\": \"never\",\n    \"comment\": \"draft\",\n    \"review\": \"draft\",\n    \"label\": \"draft\",\n    \"assign\": \"draft\",\n    \"open_issue\": \"draft\",\n    \"close\": \"never\",\n    \"merge\": \"never\",\n    \"push_code\": \"never\",\n    \"dispatch_session\": \"draft\",\n    \"create_worktree\": \"draft\"\n  },\n  \"forge\": \"github\",\n  \"collaboration\": {\n    \"templates\": false,\n    \"ci_check\": true,\n    \"ci_agent\": false,\n    \"codeowners\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"kb\": {\n    \"visibility\": \"public\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/panelarr/knowledge\"\n  },\n  \"privacy\": {\n    \"enabled\": false,\n    \"extra_patterns\": [],\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"EXTREPO\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"secrets\": false,\n  \"license\": \"own-open\",\n  \"areas\": {\n    \"add\": [],\n    \"remove\": []\n  },\n  \"git\": {\n    \"init\": true,\n    \"hooks\": true\n  },\n  \"seed\": {}\n}\n```\n\nThe seed text, if any, is IN-0002."
